ee="Arms",name=S[484],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[669],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[462],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[545],r=2,max=2},{tree="Arms",name=S[601],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[622],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name=S[602],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name="Impale",r=2,max=2},{tree="Arms",name="Bloodthrill",r=2,max=2},{tree="Arms",name=S[702],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name=S[846],r=5,max=5},{tree="Arms",name=S[832],r=2,max=2},{tree="Arms",name=S[747],r=1,max=1},{tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[623],r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[624],r=1,max=1},{tree="Fury",name=S[802],r=1,max=2},{tree="Protection",name=S[781],r=2,max=2}},order={{l1=10,l2=12,tree="Arms",name=S[484],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=13,l2=15,tree="Arms",name=S[669],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=16,l2=18,tree="Arms",name=S[462],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=19,l2=20,tree="Arms",name=S[545],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=21,l2=21,tree="Arms",name=S[601],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=22,l2=24,tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=25,l2=25,tree="Arms",name=S[622],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=28,tree="Arms",name=S[602],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=29,l2=30,tree="Arms",name="Impale",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=31,l2=32,tree="Arms",name="Bloodthrill",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=33,l2=33,tree="Arms",name=S[702],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=34,l2=38,tree="Arms",name=S[846],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=39,l2=40,tree="Arms",name=S[832],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=41,l2=41,tree="Arms",name=S[747],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=42,l2=46,tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=47,l2=51,tree="Fury",name=S[623],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=52,l2=56,tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=57,l2=57,tree="Fury",name=S[624],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=58,l2=58,tree="Fury",name=S[802],r1=1,r2=1,max=2},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Protection",name=S[781],r1=1,r2=2,max=2}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[546]},{t="p",s="legend",x="|cff71d5ffBlue text was updated for the WoW Forever hotfixes up to 10 November and is awaiting final review.|r"},{t="h1",x="Arms",sub=S[637]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Swing a slow two-hander, keep Rend on your target so Bloodthrill opens extra Overpowers, and lead with Mortal Strike from level 40. Sweeping Strikes and Cleave let you kill two enemies at once."},{t="pills",list={S[562],S[607]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[748]},{t="h2",x=S[467]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward the level-60 build. Arms fights from Battle Stance with a two-handed weapon the whole way; the stance dance only comes in for interrupts, Whirlwind and defensive cooldowns."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Rend, Overpower and Charge"},{t="p",x="Open with Charge and fight in Battle Stance with the best two-hander you can find. Improved Heroic Strike (10–12) makes Heroic Strike 3 Rage cheaper, Improved Rend (13–15) makes Rend worth its Rage, and Improved Overpower adds 50% critical strike chance to Overpower after a dodge. Do the level 10 class quest for Defensive Stance, Sunder Armor and Taunt. Tactical Mastery, trained at 14, keeps 10 Rage when you change stance; Improved Tactical Mastery (16–18) keeps up to 15 more."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Two targets at a time"},{t="p",x="Slam and Victory Rush arrive at 20. Deep Wounds (22–24) adds a bleed to your critical strikes, Spearing Strike at 25 is a cheap extra hit that does much more to Giants, Dragonkin and mounted targets, and Two-Handed Weapon Specialization (26–28) adds 6% damage with a two-hander. Bloodthrill (31–32) gives main-hand hits on a Rend target a 20% chance to enable Overpower, and Sweeping Strikes at 33 copies your next five attacks to a second enemy, so pool Rage, pull two and Cleave. Weaponmaster follows (34–38), and Improved Slam 2/2 (39–40) stops Slam from delaying your swing and shortens its cooldown."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Mortal Strike"},{t="p",x="Mortal Strike at 40 becomes your main attack and cuts healing on the target by 50%. Weaponmaster rewards whichever weapon type you hold, so pick weapons by damage per second. The last points go into Cruelty, Unbridled Wrath, Enrage, Reckless Swings (extra Rage on your next four swings for 25% of your base health) and Improved Execute in Fury, plus Improved Bloodrage in Protection. Plate armor is trained at 40."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[504]},{t="h2",x=S[562]},{t="p",x=S[65]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[569]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[485]},{t="p",x=S[119]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Arms in Forever is built around Rend: Bloodthrill turns your main-hand hits on a Rend target into extra Overpowers, so keep Rend on whatever you are hitting. Weaponmaster replaces the old weapon specializations: axes and polearms gain 5% critical strike chance, maces and staves ignore 15% of armor, and swords can trigger an extra attack. Precision no longer exists, so all of your hit comes from gear."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[660]},{t="h2",x=S[527]},{t="p",x="Your two-handed weapon is your most important item: Mortal Strike, Overpower, Slam and Whirlwind all scale with it. After that come hit, expertise, critical strike and Strength."},{t="h3",x=S[725]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x="a slow two-hander"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Strength",x=S[703]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=S[726]},{t="p",s="small",x="A slower two-hander hits harder per swing at the same damage per second. Rage from normal swings is normalized in Forever: more damage does not mean more Rage, but critical auto attacks give double Rage."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x="and speed"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5%"},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[813],x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Agility can beat Strength when an item has about 1.5 times as much of it. Haste and attack power are useful extras."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[82]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[528]},{t="h2",x=S[588]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. Before Bloodthrill at 31, Sweeping Strikes at 33 and Mortal Strike at 40, leave out the steps you have not unlocked."},{t="h4",x="Open with Charge"},{t="p",x="Keep Battle Shout up and use Bloodrage between pulls so you start with Rage. Charge from Battle Stance generates Rage and stuns for 1 second. If several enemies stand together, pull one with a ranged weapon instead."},{t="h4",x="Rend, then Overpower"},{t="p",x="Apply Rend to anything that will live through most of it, and do not refresh it on a dying target. Use Overpower the moment it lights up, after a dodge or from Bloodthrill. It costs 5 Rage, cannot be dodged, blocked or parried, and Improved Overpower gives it 50% extra critical chance. Switching targets loses the proc."},{t="h4",x="Mortal Strike on cooldown"},{t="p",x="From 40, Mortal Strike is your main attack: weapon damage plus a bonus, 30 Rage, 6-second cooldown, and 50% less healing on the target for 10 seconds. Keep enough Rage for it after Rend and Overpower."},{t="h4",x="Slam with spare Rage"},{t="p",x="Slam costs 15 Rage. Before Improved Slam, cast it straight after an auto-attack because it resets your swing. With Improved Slam it no longer interrupts or delays your swing, and at 2/2 its 15-second cooldown drops to 10 seconds."},{t="h4",x="Two enemies: Sweeping Strikes and Cleave"},{t="p",x="Pool Rage on one target, heal up, then pull two. Sweeping Strikes (30 Rage) copies your next five attacks to a second enemy|cff71d5ff, and keeps its charges when no second enemy is hit|r; Cleave and Slam are cheap ways to spend them. Put Rend on both so either can trigger Bloodthrill. Whirlwind needs Berserker Stance and is best saved for group pulls."},{t="h4",x="Execute and Heroic Strike"},{t="p",x="Execute works below 20% health and spends all your remaining Rage. While questing, let auto-attacks finish weak enemies and keep the Rage; on dungeon bosses use Execute freely. Heroic Strike and Cleave replace your next swing and stop it generating Rage, so use them only when Rage is high."},{t="abil",names={S[747],"Overpower","Rend","Slam",S[702],"Cleave","Execute","Charge"}},{t="h3",x=S[789]},{t="p",x="Weapon damage comes first: Mortal Strike, Overpower, Slam and Whirlwind all scale with it, and a slower two-hander hits harder per swing at the same damage per second. After that look for hit, critical strike, Strength and Agility. Strength gives 2 attack power per point; Agility gives critical chance, dodge and armor but no attack power for a Warrior."},{t="p",x="Use the references below as candidate lists. Warriors use every melee weapon type plus bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; you still need the weapon skill, so train it before you switch types. Plate is trained at level 40; until then mail is your heaviest armor."},{t="h3",x=S[439]},{t="p",x="Victory Rush is your only self-heal, so carry food and First Aid bandages. Sharpening stones on blades and axes, or weightstones on maces and staves, add flat damage to every hit. Rage and Strength consumables help most in dungeons."},{t="p",x="Battle Shout raises attack power for your group, Demoralizing Shout and Thunder Clap reduce the damage you take, and Sunder Armor helps every physical attacker. Shield Bash needs a shield; Pummel needs Berserker Stance from 38. Keep Hamstring for runners."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[638]},{t="h2",x=S[440]},{t="p",x=S[61]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[41]},{t="macro",n=S[498],x=S[206],code=S[268]},{t="macro",n=S[608],x=S[154],code=S[259]},{t="macro",n=S[704],x=S[326],code=S[275]},{t="macro",n=S[710],x=S[195],code=S[295]},{t="macro",n=S[589],x=S[218],code=S[253]},{t="macro",n=S[499],x=S[226],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n=S[500],x=S[156],code=S[305]},{t="macro",n="Ranged pull",x=S[237],code=S[171]},{t="macro",n=S[515],x=S[166],code=S[276]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Rend",x="Spread Rend across two targets during Sweeping Strikes so either can trigger Bloodthrill.",code="#showtooltip Rend\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Rend"},{t="macro",n="Mortal Strike / Shift Execute",x="Normal press casts Mortal Strike. Hold Shift for Execute when the target is below 20%.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Execute; [harm,nodead] Mortal Strike"},{t="macro",n="Sweeping Strikes + Cleave",x="Activates Sweeping Strikes and queues Cleave on your next swing. Cleave is a next-swing attack, so it does not wait for the global cooldown.",code="#showtooltip Sweeping Strikes\n/cast Sweeping Strikes\n/cast Cleave"},{t="macro",n="Shield up / Shift two-hander",x="Swap to a one-hander and shield for Shield Bash or Shield Wall; hold Shift to swap back. Replace the three item names with your own.",code="#showtooltip\n/equip [mod:shift] Your Two-Hander\n/equipslot [nomod] 16 Your One-Hander\n/equipslot [nomod] 17 Your Shield"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[711]},{t="h2",x=S[486]},{t="p",x=S[67]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[68]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Warrior loot selection · 30 October 2026. Mail and plate armor, shields, cloaks and jewelry, every melee weapon type, and bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; Intellect-, Spirit- and spell-only pieces are excluded. Shields are hidden on the Arms page. Rarity and acquisition confidence remain separate."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[529]},{t="h2",x=S[483]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[570]},{t="h2",x=S[468]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[530]},{t="h2",x=S[426]},{t="p",x=S[36]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[497]},{t="kicker",x=S[712]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[101]}}},{id="fury",name="Fury",token="FURY",title="Fury | WoW Forever Warrior Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[746]},{id="journey",x=S[605]},{id="talents",x=S[503]},{id="stats",x=S[658]},{id="combat",x=S[659]},{id="macros",x=S[636]},{id="dungeons",x=S[568]},{id="professions",x=S[606]},{id="crafting",x=S[587]},{id="questgear",x=S[544]},{id=S[497],x=S[709]}},asideNote=S[83],talentString="30303213102000000050530055102100231",ranks={{tree="Arms",name=S[484],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[669],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[462],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[545],r=2,max=2},{tree="Arms",name=S[601],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[622],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name="Impale",r=2,max=2},{tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[623],r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[790],r=3,max=3},{tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[691],r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[624],r=1,max=1},{tree="Fury",name=S[708],r=2,max=2},{tree="Fury",name="Death Wish",r=1,max=1},{tree="Fury",name=S[782],r=2,max=2},{tree="Fury",name="Flurry",r=3,max=3},{tree="Fury",name="Bloodthirst",r=1,max=1}},order={{l1=10,l2=12,tree="Arms",name=S[484],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=13,l2=15,tree="Arms",name=S[669],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=16,l2=18,tree="Arms",name=S[462],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=19,l2=20,tree="Arms",name=S[545],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=21,l2=21,tree="Arms",name=S[601],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=22,l2=24,tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=25,l2=25,tree="Arms",name=S[622],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=27,tree="Arms",name="Impale",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=28,l2=32,tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=33,l2=37,tree="Fury",name=S[623],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=38,l2=40,tree="Fury",name=S[790],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Fury",name=S[691],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=51,l2=51,tree="Fury",name=S[624],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=52,l2=53,tree="Fury",name=S[708],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=54,l2=54,tree="Fury",name="Death Wish",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=55,l2=56,tree="Fury",name=S[782],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=57,l2=59,tree="Fury",name="Flurry",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=60,l2=60,tree="Fury",name="Bloodthirst",r1=1,r2=1,max=1}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[546]},{t="h1",x="Fury",sub=S[637]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Dual wield from level 20, gain Rage from both weapons, and hit with Whirlwind and Bloodthirst from Berserker Stance, with Reckless Swings and Death Wish for extra Rage and burst."},{t="pills",list={S[563],S[607]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[748]},{t="h2",x=S[467]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward the level-60 build. Warriors learn Dual Wield at 20, so Fury uses a two-hander until then. From level 40 you can keep Protection as a second specialization for tanking."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Rend, Overpower and Rage"},{t="p",x="Use a two-hander in Battle Stance with Charge, Rend and Overpower. The first points go into Arms: Improved Heroic Strike (10–12), Improved Rend (13–15), Improved Tactical Mastery (16–18) to keep more Rage when you change stance, and Improved Overpower (19–20). Do the level 10 class quest for Defensive Stance, Sunder Armor and Taunt. Tactical Mastery, trained at 14, keeps 10 Rage when you change stance."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Two weapons"},{t="p",x="Train Dual Wield at 20. Anger Management (21), Deep Wounds (22–24), Spearing Strike (25) and Impale (26–27) finish the Arms points, then Cruelty (28–32) adds 5% critical strike chance, Unbridled Wrath (33–37) gives your weapon hits a chance to generate extra Rage, and Furious Precision (38–40) adds up to 10% hit to off-hand attacks. Berserker Stance comes from your level 30 class quest, Whirlwind is trained at 36 and Pummel at 38."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Bloodthirst"},{t="p",x="Enrage (41–45) and Dual Wield Specialization (46–50, 50% more off-hand damage) come next, then Reckless Swings (51), Improved Berserker Rage (52–53), Death Wish (54), Improved Whirlwind (55–56, a shorter cooldown and more damage to the closest enemy) and Flurry (57–59, 30% attack speed for three swings after a critical strike). Bloodthirst completes the build at 60. Plate armor is trained at 40."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[504]},{t="h2",x=S[563]},{t="p",x=S[65]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[569]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[485]},{t="p",x=S[119]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Off-hand attacks miss much more often than main-hand ones, which is why Furious Precision exists: it adds 10% hit to off-hand attacks only. Whirlwind already strikes with both weapons in Forever, and Improved Whirlwind shortens its cooldown by 2 seconds and adds 30% damage to the closest enemy. Reckless Swings costs 25% of your base health for 5 extra Rage on each of your next four swings."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[660]},{t="h2",x=S[527]},{t="p",x="Fury wants strong weapons first, then hit and expertise so your attacks land, then critical strike and Strength. Crits also feed Flurry and Rage."},{t="h3",x=S[725]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Strength",x=S[703]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=S[726]},{t="p",s="small",x="Rage from normal swings is normalized in Forever: more damage does not mean more Rage, but critical auto attacks give double Rage."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5% from behind"},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[813],x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Weapon skill is rare in Forever but very strong when you find it; some estimates put it first, up to 305. Dual wielding raises the miss chance of white hits, so extra hit still helps."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[82]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[528]},{t="h2",x=S[588]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. Before Dual Wield at 20, Whirlwind at 36 and Bloodthirst at 60, leave out the steps you have not unlocked."},{t="h4",x="Charge, then Berserker Stance"},{t="p",x="Keep Battle Shout up and use Bloodrage between pulls. Charge from Battle Stance, then switch to Berserker Stance: Tactical Mastery keeps up to 10 Rage through the switch, and the stance adds 3% critical strike chance but 10% more damage taken."},{t="h4",x="Bloodthirst on cooldown"},{t="p",x="From 60, Bloodthirst (30 Rage, 6-second cooldown) deals damage equal to 45% of your attack power plus a flat amount, and gives 10% movement speed for 10 seconds."},{t="h4",x="Whirlwind on cooldown"},{t="p",x="Whirlwind (25 Rage, 10-second cooldown, 8 seconds with Improved Whirlwind, Berserker Stance) hits up to four enemies within 8 yards with both weapons. Use it on single targets too once Bloodthirst is on cooldown. Before 36, keep Rend and Overpower from Battle Stance instead."},{t="h4",x="Overpower after a dodge"},{t="p",x="When the target dodges, swap to Battle Stance and use Overpower; Improved Overpower gives it 50% extra critical chance. Swap back afterwards. Only do this when the stance change will not throw away pooled Rage."},{t="h4",x="Execute and spare Rage"},{t="p",x="Execute works below 20% health and spends all your remaining Rage, so use it when it will kill or on a boss. With Rage to spare, queue Heroic Strike, or Cleave on two targets; both replace a swing and stop it generating Rage."},{t="h4",x="Cooldowns"},{t="p",x="Death Wish adds 20% Physical damage and Fear immunity for 30 seconds but raises damage taken by 5%. Berserker Rage breaks Fear and Incapacitate and gives extra Rage from hits taken. Recklessness at 50 doubles your critical strike chance for 15 seconds at the cost of 20% more damage taken. Piercing Howl slows everything nearby when you need to get away."},{t="abil",names={"Bloodthirst","Whirlwind","Execute","Heroic Strike","Death Wish","Berserker Rage","Intercept","Pummel"}},{t="h3",x=S[789]},{t="p",x="Weapon damage per second comes first on both weapons. A slow main hand makes Bloodthirst-free swings and Whirlwind hit harder; the off hand can be faster. Hit matters more for Fury than any other Warrior build because off-hand attacks miss so often, then critical strike for Flurry and Enrage, then Strength and Agility."},{t="p",x="Use the references below as candidate lists. Main Hand weapons cannot go in your off hand; pair them with a One-Hand weapon. Plate is trained at level 40; until then mail is your heaviest armor."},{t="h3",x=S[439]},{t="p",x="Victory Rush gives you some healing in fights, but food and bandages still cover the gaps. Keep sharpening stones or weightstones on both weapons. Rage potions help most during Death Wish and Recklessness."},{t="p",x="Battle Shout raises attack power for your group and Demoralizing Shout reduces damage taken. Pummel works in Berserker Stance without a shield from 38; before that, equip a shield for Shield Bash. Intercept closes gaps in combat from 30."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[638]},{t="h2",x=S[440]},{t="p",x=S[61]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[41]},{t="macro",n=S[498],x=S[206],code=S[268]},{t="macro",n=S[608],x=S[154],code=S[259]},{t="macro",n=S[704],x=S[326],code=S[275]},{t="macro",n=S[710],x=S[195],code=S[295]},{t="macro",n=S[589],x=S[218],code=S[253]},{t="macro",n=S[499],x=S[226],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n=S[500],x=S[156],code=S[305]},{t="macro",n="Ranged pull",x=S[237],code=S[171]},{t="macro",n=S[515],x=S[166],code=S[276]},{t="macro",n="Whirlwind / switch to Berserker",x="In Berserker Stance this casts Whirlwind. In any other stance the first press switches stance; press again to Whirlwind.",code="#showtooltip Whirlwind\n/cast [stance:3] Whirlwind; Berserker Stance"},{t="macro",n="Bloodthirst / Shift Execute",x="Normal press casts Bloodthirst. Hold Shift for Execute when the target is below 20%.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Execute; [harm,nodead] Bloodthirst"},{t="macro",n="Bloodrage into Death Wish",x="Bloodrage first for the Rage, then Death Wish. If Bloodrage is on cooldown the macro still casts Death Wish.",code="#showtooltip Death Wish\n/cast Bloodrage\n/cast Death Wish"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Hamstring",x="Slow a runner under your pointer without changing targets, before it reaches more enemies.",code="#showtooltip Hamstring\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Hamstring"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[711]},{t="h2",x=S[486]},{t="p",x=S[67]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[68]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Warrior loot selection · 30 October 2026. Mail and plate armor, shields, cloaks and jewelry, every melee weapon type, and bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; Intellect-, Spirit- and spell-only pieces are excluded. Shields are hidden on the Fury page. Rarity and acquisition confidence remain separate."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[529]},{t="h2",x=S[483]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[570]},{t="h2",x=S[468]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[530]},{t="h2",x=S[426]},{t="p",x=S[36]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[497]},{t="kicker",x=S[712]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[101]}}},{id="protection",name="Protection",token="PROT",title="Protection | WoW Forever Warrior Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[746]},{id="journey",x=S[605]},{id="talents",x=S[503]},{id="stats",x=S[658]},{id="combat",x=S[659]},{id="macros",x=S[636]},{id="dungeons",x=S[568]},{id="professions",x=S[606]},{id="crafting",x=S[587]},{id="questgear",x=S[544]},{id=S[497],x=S[709]}},asideNote=S[83],talentString="05000000000000000055000050000000000050530120301021251",ranks={{tree="Arms",name="Deflection",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[826],r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r=5,max=5},{tree="Protection",name=S[727],r=5,max=5},{tree="Protection",name=S[847],r=5,max=5},{tree="Protection",name=S[803],r=3,max=3},{tree="Protection",name="Last Stand",r=1,max=1},{tree="Protection",name=S[791],r=2,max=2},{tree="Protection",name="Defiance",r=3,max=3},{tree="Protection",name="Vanguard",r=1,max=1},{tree="Protection",name=S[740],r=2,max=2},{tree="Protection",name=S[713],r=1,max=1},{tree="Protection",name=S[848],r=2,max=3},{tree="Protection",name="Bastion",r=5,max=5},{tree="Protection",name="Shield Slam",r=1,max=1}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="Protection",name=S[727],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=19,tree="Protection",name=S[847],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=20,l2=20,tree="Protection",name="Last Stand",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=21,l2=22,tree="Protection",name=S[791],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=23,l2=25,tree="Protection",name=S[803],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=26,l2=28,tree="Protection",name="Defiance",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=29,l2=29,tree="Protection",name="Vanguard",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=30,l2=31,tree="Protection",name=S[740],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=32,l2=32,tree="Protection",name=S[713],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=33,l2=34,tree="Protection",name=S[848],r1=1,r2=2,max=3},{l1=35,l2=39,tree="Protection",name="Bastion",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Protection",name="Shield Slam",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Arms",name="Deflection",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=51,l2=55,tree="Fury",name=S[826],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=56,l2=60,tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r1=1,r2=5,max=5}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[546]},{t="h1",x="Protection",sub=S[637]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Level with a one-hander and shield in Defensive Stance: blocks, dodges and parries feed you Rage, Revenge and Shield Slam hit hard, and you can tank every dungeon you reach."},{t="pills",list={S[564],S[607]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[748]},{t="h2",x=S[467]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward the level-60 build. Protection is the stronger leveling build up to about 40, especially if you also tank dungeons. From 40 you can add Fury as a second specialization for open-world questing."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Shield and Rage"},{t="p",x="Equip a one-hander and shield as soon as you can. Shield Specialization reaches 5/5 at 14: more block chance and 5 Rage every time you block. Do the level 10 class quest for Defensive Stance, Sunder Armor and Taunt. Anticipation (15–19) adds Defense, and Shield Block at 16 helps you block more often."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Vanguard and Bastion"},{t="p",x="Last Stand arrives at 20 and Master of Defense (21–22) gives Rage when you dodge or parry with a shield. Improved Revenge (23–25) makes Revenge a cheap, hard-hitting attack and Defiance (26–28) adds threat. Vanguard at 29 lets you Charge in Defensive Stance, so you can stay in it full time. Improved Shield Wall (30–31), Concussion Blow at 32 and Focused Rage (33–34) follow, then Bastion (35–39) for 10% more damage with a shield."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Shield Slam"},{t="p",x="Shield Slam at 40 is your strongest attack and scales with your block value. The last 20 points go into Deflection in Arms (41–45), then Cruelty, Lingering Rage and Enrage in Fury. Plate armor is trained at 40."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[504]},{t="h2",x=S[564]},{t="p",x=S[65]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[569]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[485]},{t="p",x=S[119]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Bastion adds 10% to all damage you deal and Defiance adds 20% threat in Defensive Stance, but both only while a shield is equipped, so keep the shield on even when questing. Shield Specialization and Master of Defense turn blocks, dodges and parries into Rage, which makes Protection self-sufficient while leveling. Improved Shield Wall 2/2 shortens Shield Wall’s cooldown."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[660]},{t="h2",x=S[527]},{t="p",x="Protection balances two lists: stats that make your attacks land for threat, and stats that keep you alive. Start balanced and lean defensive for hard-hitting bosses."},{t="h3",x=S[725]},{t="stat",i=1,b="Armor",x="shield and heavy armor"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Strength",x="threat and block value"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Defense",x="fewer crits taken"},{t="stat",i=5,b=S[596],x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Keep a two-hander or dual-wield set for questing alone, and a shield set for dungeons."},{t="h3",x="At level 60: threat"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5%, then 14% from the front"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Strength",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Agility gives armor, dodge and crit, which makes it one of the best tank stats overall."},{t="h3",x="At level 60: survival"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Armor",x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Agility",x="dodge and armor"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Avoidance",x="dodge and parry"},{t="stat",i=5,b="Defense",x="to 440"},{t="p",s="small",x="Shield Block also prevents critical hits, so Defense matters a little less for Warriors than for other tanks. Some estimates still put Defense to 440 second."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Melee hit cap: 8% for special attacks against raid bosses. Expertise removes dodge at 6.5% and parry at 14% (parry only matters from the front). Defense 440 makes a level 63 boss unable to land a critical hit on you. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[528]},{t="h2",x=S[588]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. Before Vanguard at 29, Concussion Blow at 32 and Shield Slam at 40, leave out the steps you have not unlocked."},{t="h4",x="Open in Defensive Stance"},{t="p",x="Keep Battle Shout up and use Bloodrage between pulls. From 29, Vanguard lets you Charge straight from Defensive Stance; before that, Charge in Battle Stance and switch. Defensive Stance cuts damage taken and dealt by 10% and adds 80% threat."},{t="h4",x="Shield Slam on cooldown"},{t="p",x="From 40, Shield Slam (20 Rage, 6-second cooldown) is your hardest hit and highest threat. Its damage rises with your block value, and it has a 50% chance to dispel a magic effect on the target."},{t="h4",x="Revenge whenever it lights up"},{t="p",x="Revenge becomes usable after you block, dodge or parry. It costs 5 Rage, has a 5-second cooldown and causes high threat; Improved Revenge adds 60% damage. Pair it with Sunder Armor in one button (see the macros)."},{t="h4",x="Shield Block for Rage"},{t="p",x="Shield Block (10 Rage, 5-second cooldown) raises block chance by 75% for 7 seconds, up to two blocks. Every block feeds Shield Specialization’s 5 Rage and enables Revenge, so use it often while tanking and questing."},{t="h4",x="Packs"},{t="p",x="Thunder Clap now works in Defensive Stance: it hits up to four enemies and slows their attacks by 20%. Add Demoralizing Shout, spread Sunder Armor with a mouseover macro, and Taunt anything that turns to a group member. Challenging Shout pulls everything back for 6 seconds in an emergency."},{t="h4",x="Emergencies"},{t="p",x="Last Stand grants 30% of your maximum health for 20 seconds. Shield Wall cuts damage taken by 60% for 12 seconds. Concussion Blow stuns for 5 seconds, and Shield Bash interrupts a cast. Retaliation and Shield Wall no longer share a cooldown."},{t="abil",names={"Shield Slam","Revenge","Shield Block","Sunder Armor","Thunder Clap","Taunt","Demoralizing Shout",S[713]}},{t="h3",x="Equipment and threat"},{t="p",x="Armor and Stamina come first for tanking, then Defense, Dodge, Parry and Block. Block value matters more than in Classic because it raises Shield Slam’s damage. While leveling solo, weapon damage per second and Strength still decide how fast you kill."},{t="p",x="Use the references below as candidate lists. Pick a one-handed weapon that can go in the main hand and the best shield you can find. Plate is trained at level 40; until then mail is your heaviest armor."},{t="h3",x=S[439]},{t="p",x="Protection takes less damage than other Warriors while leveling, but you still need food and bandages; Victory Rush helps in fights. Keep a sharpening stone or weightstone on your weapon for threat."},{t="p",x="Battle Shout and Booming Voice cover your group. Thunder Clap and Demoralizing Shout reduce the damage you take from packs. Taunt has an 8-second cooldown; Mocking Blow and Challenging Shout are your backups."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[638]},{t="h2",x=S[440]},{t="p",x=S[61]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[41]},{t="macro",n=S[498],x="With Vanguard you can Charge from Battle or Defensive Stance out of combat. In Berserker Stance this Intercepts (from 30).",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [nocombat,stance:1/2] Charge; [stance:3] Intercept"},{t="macro",n=S[608],x=S[154],code=S[259]},{t="macro",n=S[704],x=S[326],code=S[275]},{t="macro",n=S[710],x=S[195],code=S[295]},{t="macro",n=S[589],x=S[218],code=S[253]},{t="macro",n=S[499],x=S[226],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n=S[500],x=S[156],code=S[305]},{t="macro",n="Ranged pull",x=S[237],code=S[171]},{t="macro",n=S[515],x=S[166],code=S[276]},{t="macro",n="Revenge, otherwise Sunder",x="Casts Revenge when it is available; otherwise the same press casts Sunder Armor. One button for most of your threat.",code="#showtooltip Revenge\n/cast Revenge\n/cast Sunder Armor"},{t="macro",n="Shield Slam / Shift Shield Block",x="Normal press casts Shield Slam. Hold Shift for Shield Block to set up blocks, Rage and Revenge.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift] Shield Block; [harm,nodead] Shield Slam"},{t="macro",n="Last Stand + Shield Wall",x="Emergency button. Last Stand first for the extra health, then Shield Wall if you are in Defensive Stance.",code="#showtooltip Shield Wall\n/cast Last Stand\n/cast [stance:2] Shield Wall"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Concussion Blow",x="Stun a dangerous enemy under your pointer for 5 seconds without changing your tanking target.",code="#showtooltip Concussion Blow\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Concussion Blow"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[711]},{t="h2",x=S[486]},{t="p",x=S[67]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[68]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Warrior loot selection · 30 October 2026. Mail and plate armor, shields, cloaks and jewelry, every melee weapon type, and bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; Intellect-, Spirit- and spell-only pieces are excluded. Two-handed weapons are hidden on the Protection page. Rarity and acquisition confidence remain separate."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[529]},{t="h2",x=S[483]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[570]},{t="h2",x=S[468]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[530]},{t="h2",x=S[426]},{t="p",x=S[36]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[497]},{t="kicker",x=S[712]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[101]}}}},dungeons={{n=S[639],lr="13–18",st=S[155],no=S[25],ba=true,ra={ck=S[230],r={},t={},no={S[51],S[231],S[38]}}},{n=S[399],lr="13–18",st=S[155],no=S[25],ba=true,ra={ck=S[230],r={},t={},no={S[51],S[231],S[38]}}},{n=S[194],lr="15–20",st=S[155],no=S[25],ba=true,ra={ck=S[230],r={{n="Lordaeron Captain",st=S[94],no=S[110],it={}}},t={{id=286981,n=S[814],mob=S[21],st=S[670],no=S[20]}},no={S[112],S[56],S[38]}}},{n=S[256],lr="17–24",st=S[155],no=S[25],ba=true,ra={ck=S[230],r={{n="Deviate Faerie Dragon",st=S[94],no=S[110],it={}}},t={},no={S[112],S[231],S[38]}}},{n=S[193],lr="17–26",st=S[155],no=S[25],ba=true,ra={ck=S[230],r={{n=S[741],st=S[94],no=S[321],it={{id=5443,n=S[750]},{id=5444,n=S[834]}}}},t={{id=1951,n=S[769],mob=S[21],st=S[28],no=S[20]}},no={S[112],S[56],S[38]}}},{n=S[208],lr="22–30",st=S[155],no=S[25],ba=true,ra={ck=S[230],r={{n="Deathsworn Captain",st=S[94],no=S[110],it={}},{